nat44-ed: choose the pool address of the egress interface

With the output feature on more than one interface, ED is meant to take
the pool address bound to the egress interface. Addresses added without a
tenant VRF (fib_index ~0) -- which is what "nat44 add interface address"
and plain "nat44 add address" create -- were never bound to their
interface, because binding required the interface FIB to equal the
address's fib_index, and the selection only compared the egress for
tenant-VRF addresses. Those addresses were only fallbacks picked by a
hash of the source address, so a client could leave one exit with
another exit's address and lose all replies.

Bind addresses without a tenant VRF to the outside interface that has
them (on address add, on output/outside enable and on interface address
change), start them unbound (sw_if_index ~0 instead of 0), unbind on
interface address delete, and let the output feature prefer the bound
address for them too. Verified with two exits (WAN 192.168.1.6 by DHCP and
a tap 10.99.0.1): every client now leaves each exit with that exit's
address; before, half the clients pinged the internet with the tap's
address and got no reply.

